module askflow

// Fixture for `mara ask` interprocedural forward slicing (slice.odin).
// Not auto-checked for query output (the harness only gates compile pass/fail),
// but a stable, predictable target to validate the hop machinery by hand. From a
// dir whose name is `askflow`:  mara ask n in driver below  yields
//   n  ->  the return + 2 statements + 3 calls
//     decl    m              (consume's computed `x + 1` data-depends on n)
//     decl    k              (forward returns its first arg -> k traces to n)
//   into calls — the value lands in (4 parameters)
//     consume (param x : i64)         n flows into consume
//     forward (param a : i64)         n flows into forward's first arg
//     forward (param b : i64)         n -> m (via consume) -> forward's second arg
//     mutate  (param p : ^i64)        the bare-call pointer hop
// What this pins down:
//   * a value passed into a callee param IS a landing — whether or not the call's
//     result is bound, and whether or not the return carries it back. consume and
//     forward bind their result yet still land, the same rule that makes a glyph's
//     w/h land in pack_rect, whose return is a skyline slot, not the glyph (see
//     collect_landings). The bare pointer call mutate(&n) lands the same way;
//   * landings match the arg's REACHING DEF, not its binding, so a landing names
//     the value actually flowing into that arg at that site — an earlier or
//     other-field write to the same binding is not dragged in (slice.odin
//     flow_targets / arg_reads_targets);
//   * the STATEMENT trace is a separate data-dependence view (cg.return_deps, not
//     escape's aliasing cg.return_args): n reaches BOTH m and k, since consume's
//     computed `x + 1` traces back to n exactly as forward's identity `return a`;
//   * that return trace stays PRECISE, not a blunt "all args": forward returns
//     only `a`, so `mara ask m in driver below` shows NO `decl k` — m feeds
//     forward's IGNORED second param and never reaches k. m's only effect is the
//     landing in forward.b: it flows in, but nothing comes back.

mutate  :: fun(p: ^i64)          { p^ = 5 }
consume :: fun(x: i64) -> i64    { return x + 1 }    // computed return: data-depends on x, aliases nothing
forward :: fun(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 { return a }   // identity return of its FIRST arg (b ignored)

driver :: fun() -> i64 {
	n := 10
	mutate(&n)          // bare call, by pointer -> n lands in mutate.p
	m := consume(n)     // result bound; computed return now traces m back to n (data-dep)
	k := forward(n, m)  // returns a -> k traces to n (def->def), b (=m) ignored
	return k
}

main :: fun() -> i64 {
	return driver()
}
